{"gold":[{"independent_answer":"20","question_sha256":"fe6d29c341f951d6e5e743b8cae0ca8264c61efd74b80719b6da0360bf243c7c","reason":"The total is 17 + 20 + 23 = 60 billboards over 3 hours, and 60 / 3 = 20. This unambiguously equals the provided gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-1879"},{"independent_answer":"30","question_sha256":"5e175f65df186c400477c002089e4a61669c130f3d4c134611592d7703144fd9","reason":"Ten minutes is 10/60 = 1/6 hour, so the required speed is 5 / (1/6) = 30 mph. This equals the provided gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-735"},{"independent_answer":"360","question_sha256":"9e4d1e4829ad4937d00ee7fc6188b6055451e42c011f020650c4edd08ef3eb4c","reason":"Fiona accounts for 1 - 1/4 = 3/4 of the 8 hours: (3/4) × 8 = 6 hours. Converting gives 6 × 60 = 360 minutes, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-5808"},{"independent_answer":"66","question_sha256":"b0dd2eb2d353feb15e65faa0a0cedc3511c518de3b3d9e1b3cc22c07b2eed939","reason":"The fine represents 256 / 16 = 16 mph over the limit. Adding that to 50 mph gives 50 + 16 = 66 mph, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-4854"},{"independent_answer":"3 or 4","question_sha256":"221b5deb96d40c07f1b4998216d05e464922b8d5e6b856cef7f44821149da818","reason":"If “3 times further away” means three times as far, the time is 2 × 3 / 2 = 3 hours, matching the gold. If interpreted literally as three original distances farther, the destination is four times as far and the time is 2 × 4 / 2 = 4 hours. The wording is therefore interpretation-dependent.","status":"AMBIGUOUS","task_id":"gsm8k-train-3605"},{"independent_answer":"55","question_sha256":"bfd70b6d8b099b4ec8c63b84cc48a931266b084c21e18a06a28a87029eadaa6d","reason":"The cats' rates are 3, 2 × 3 = 6, and 6 / 3 = 2 meows per minute. Their combined rate is 11 per minute, so in 5 minutes they make 11 × 5 = 55 meows, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-127"},{"independent_answer":"252/11","question_sha256":"d170253b726cad0dfe8401c968dddab057a3321c90fdc0ed7f14254dc39adb7c","reason":"The leak operates during both on and off minutes. An on minute adds a net 12 - 1 = 11 liters and an off minute loses 1 liter, so each completed two-minute cycle nets 10 liters. After 22 minutes the tub holds 110 liters; during the next on interval it needs 10/11 minute to gain the remaining 10 liters. It first fills at 22 + 10/11 = 252/11 minutes, not 24.","status":"INVALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-708"},{"independent_answer":"50","question_sha256":"cac69010c5e3ff8641b60ee0c59fb56a518b04e188bf53a3303bad3aacd2a9cc","reason":"The superhero's hourly distance is (10 / 4) × 60 = 150 miles. The difference from 100 miles in one hour is 150 - 100 = 50 miles, equal to the gold.","status":"VALID","task_id":"gsm8k-train-7311"}],"reviews":[{"checkable_expectation":true,"evidence_spans":["I need to add up the total number of billboards seen and then divide by the number of hours.","Total billboards seen = 17 + 20 + 23 = 60 billboards.","= 60 / 3\n= 20 billboards per hour."],"first_person":true,"full_text_read":true,"grounded_operations":true,"key":"gsm8k-train-1879:rich","neutral_prefix_compatible":true,"no_padding":true,"prefix_reason":"The target uses only the three counts and number of hours supplied by the student question. Its first-person operation, sum, division, and result are explicitly verifiable without any external event or hidden feedback.","raw_call_sha256":"2c898b2d04e411dd4ece43016381da94979f2a363ba4d80de4efcc1b79fdf363","reason":"The response gives a substantive first-person choice of the averaging operation, correctly computes 17 + 20 + 23 = 60 and 60 / 3 = 20, and supplies meaningful numerical intermediates. The sum-then-divide method is reusable and the text remains relevant.","reusable_content":true,"status":"PASS","student_prefix_sha256":"e02ebfbe6618d65aacad0328660eebf621bbfcaa3ea6452d7a2313f6fa502a30","target_sha256":"68dbf9f1a8f85557aeaea01ede1ef4e9c2f5b01475370